=These bank lines were not allocated, or were allocated with something left over:

{{ $json.rows.map(r => r.line).join('\n\n') }}

Everything else this morning went straight onto the invoices. Fixing one of these is usually one cell: the customer name on the payment row, or the invoice number in the reference.

parameters.jsCode:
// What came back. A chaser that goes out and is never read again is a chaser
// that will go out again next week saying the same thing, to somebody who has
// already answered it.
//
// The model above reads what the customer wants. It is not asked the one
// question that matters most here - is this a human at all - because the
// answer is in the headers, and a model that is right 95% of the time about
// out-of-office replies is a model that stops one chase in twenty for a
// fortnight while somebody is on holiday. RFC 3834 exists: Auto-Submitted,
// Precedence, X-Autoreply. They are checked first, and they win.
//
// The dates are checked too. "We will pay on the 30th" is worth writing down;
// a date in the past, or eight months out, is not a promise, it is a sentence
// with a number in it, and it goes to a person instead.

const cfg = $('Set Reply Rules').first().json;
const read = $input.all();

// Le email si ripescano dal trigger per nome, non dall'ingresso di questo
// nodo: quello che arriva qui e' l'uscita dell'estrattore, che ha gia'
// buttato via l'intestazione, ed e' l'intestazione a dire se ha scritto una
// persona. Stesso ordine, stesso indice.
let emails = [];
try {
  emails = $('When a Reply Arrives').all();
} catch (e) {
  emails = [];                       // esecuzione a mano, senza la posta
}

const DAY = 86400000;
const maxPromise = Number(cfg.max_promise_days) || 45;
const INTENTS = ['promise', 'dispute', 'paid', 'copy', 'other'];

const today = new Date();
today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

function calendarDay(value) {
  const s = String(value == null ? '' : value).trim();
  if (!s) return null;
  let m = s.match(/^(\d{4})-(\d{1,2})-(\d{1,2})/);
  if (m) return new Date(Number(m[1]), Number(m[2]) - 1, Number(m[3])).getTime();
  m = s.match(/^(\d{1,2})[/.-](\d{1,2})[/.-](\d{4})$/);
  if (m) {
    const a = Number(m[1]);
    const b = Number(m[2]);
    const dayFirst = a > 12 ? true : b > 12 ? false : String(cfg.date_order) !== 'MDY';
    return new Date(Number(m[3]), (dayFirst ? b : a) - 1, dayFirst ? a : b).getTime();
  }
  const d = new Date(s);
  return isNaN(d.getTime()) ? null : new Date(d.getFullYear(), d.getMonth(), d.getDate()).getTime();
}

const iso = (t) => {
  const d = new Date(t);
  const pad = (n) => String(n).padStart(2, '0');
  return `${d.getFullYear()}-${pad(d.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(d.getDate())}`;
};

// RFC 3834 and what the rest of the world does instead of it.
function automatic(meta) {
  // Gmail restituisce le intestazioni come oggetto; qualche versione le da'
  // come lista di {name, value}, e la maiuscola non e' garantita in nessuna
  // delle due. Si normalizza una volta sola.
  const raw = meta.headers || {};
  const pairs = Array.isArray(raw) ? raw.map((h) => [h.name, h.value]) : Object.entries(raw);
  const headers = {};
  for (const [name, value] of pairs) {
    headers[String(name).toLowerCase()] = String(value == null ? '' : value).trim().toLowerCase();
  }
  const header = (name) => headers[name] || '';

  const submitted = header('auto-submitted');
  if (submitted && submitted !== 'no') return `the Auto-Submitted: ${submitted} header`;
  if (header('x-autoreply') || header('x-autorespond') || header('x-auto-response-suppress')) {
    return 'an auto-responder header';
  }
  const precedence = header('precedence');
  if (['bulk', 'auto_reply', 'list', 'junk'].includes(precedence)) {
    return `the Precedence: ${precedence} header`;
  }

  const subject = String(meta.subject || '').toLowerCase()
    .replace(/^((re|fwd?|aw|sv|vs|antwort)\s*:\s*)+/g, '').trim();
  if (/^(auto(matic)?[ -]?(reply|response|answer)|autoreply|out of (the )?office|ooo\b|absence|undeliverable|undelivered|delivery status notification|mail delivery (failed|subsystem))/.test(subject)) {
    return 'the subject line';
  }
  const opening = String(meta.text || meta.snippet || '').slice(0, 500).toLowerCase();
  if (/\b(out of the office|away from the office|on annual leave|on holiday until|on parental leave|currently away|will be back on)\b/.test(opening)) {
    return 'the opening lines of the reply';
  }
  return '';
}

// Invoice numbers: the ones the model listed, plus the ones a pattern can see
// in the subject and the body. Both, because the model misses the number in a
// quoted footer and the pattern misses "the one from March".
//
// The pattern allows no space between the letters and the digits, and throws
// currency codes away. "EUR 2000.00" is in the subject line of every chaser
// this workflow sends, and read as an invoice number it puts a dispute on an
// invoice that does not exist. That is not a hypothetical: it is what this
// line did before it was written this way, and what the checks hold it to.
const CURRENCY = /^(eur|usd|gbp|chf|sek|nok|dkk|pln|czk|huf|ron|aud|cad|jpy|inr|nzd|zar)$/i;

function invoiceNumbers(listed, text) {
  const found = new Set();
  for (const raw of String(listed || '').split(/[,;\s]+/)) {
    const n = raw.trim().replace(/[.,;:]+$/, '');
    if (n.length >= 3 && /\d/.test(n)) found.add(n.toUpperCase());
  }
  for (const m of String(text || '').matchAll(/\b([A-Z]{2,5})([-/]?\d{2,10}(?:[-/]\d{1,10})*)\b/gi)) {
    if (CURRENCY.test(m[1])) continue;
    found.add(`${m[1]}${m[2]}`.toUpperCase());
  }
  return [...found].slice(0, 20);
}

const out = [];

read.forEach((item, index) => {
  const said = item.json.output || item.json;
  const meta = (emails[index] || emails[0] || { json: {} }).json;
  const body = `${meta.subject || ''}\n${meta.text || meta.snippet || ''}`;

  const from = String(meta.from || '').trim();
  const subject = String(meta.subject || '').trim();
  const base = {
    from,
    subject,
    received_at: String(meta.date || '').trim(),
    message_id: String(meta.id || '').trim(),
    thread_id: String(meta.threadId || '').trim(),
    intent: INTENTS.includes(String(said.intent || '').toLowerCase())
      ? String(said.intent).toLowerCase() : 'other',
    summary: String(said.summary || '').trim(),
    quoted_invoices: '',
    promised_on: '',
    dispute_reason: '',
    invoice_number: '',
  };

  const robot = automatic(meta);
  if (robot) {
    out.push({ json: { ...base, action: 'ignore', intent: 'auto-reply',
      why: `an automatic reply, and ${robot} says so. Nobody has answered yet, so the `
        + 'chase ladder is left exactly where it was' } });
    return;
  }

  const numbers = invoiceNumbers(said.invoice_numbers, body);
  base.quoted_invoices = numbers.join(', ');

  const handOver = (why, extra) => {
    out.push({ json: { ...base, action: 'follow-up', why,
      detail: [extra, base.summary ? `They say: ${base.summary}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join('\n') } });
  };

  if (base.intent === 'promise') {
    const when = calendarDay(said.promised_date);
    if (when === null) {
      handOver('they promise to pay but the date could not be read',
        `What they wrote: "${String(said.promised_date || '').trim() || 'nothing'}"`);
      return;
    }
    const days = Math.round((when - today.getTime()) / DAY);
    if (days < 0) {
      handOver(`the date they gave, ${iso(when)}, has already gone`,
        'Either it was paid and nobody matched it, or the promise is already broken');
      return;
    }
    if (days > maxPromise) {
      handOver(`they promise ${iso(when)}, which is ${days} days out`,
        `Anything past ${maxPromise} days is a payment plan, not a promise: somebody should agree it`);
      return;
    }
    if (!numbers.length) {
      handOver('they give a date but name no invoice', 'Write the date on the right rows by hand');
      return;
    }
    for (const number of numbers) {
      out.push({ json: { ...base, action: 'promise', invoice_number: number,
        promised_on: iso(when),
        why: `promised for ${iso(when)}, ${days} day(s) from today. No chaser goes out on this `
          + 'invoice until that date has passed' } });
    }
    return;
  }

  if (base.intent === 'dispute') {
    const reason = String(said.dispute_reason || '').trim() || base.summary || 'no reason given';
    if (!numbers.length) {
      handOver('they dispute something but name no invoice', `Their words: ${reason}`);
      return;
    }
    for (const number of numbers) {
      out.push({ json: { ...base, action: 'dispute', invoice_number: number,
        dispute_reason: reason,
        why: 'in dispute: chasing stops here, and it is the account manager who answers next' } });
    }
    return;
  }

  if (base.intent === 'paid') {
    handOver('they say it is already paid',
      [`Reference: ${String(said.payment_reference || '').trim() || 'not given'}`,
       `Paid on: ${String(said.payment_date || '').trim() || 'not given'}`,
       numbers.length ? `Invoice(s): ${numbers.join(', ')}` : 'No invoice number given',
       'Check the bank lines before answering: if it is there, the matching run missed it'].join('\n'));
    return;
  }

  if (base.intent === 'copy') {
    handOver('they are asking for a copy or a statement',
      numbers.length ? `Invoice(s): ${numbers.join(', ')}` : 'They do not say which invoice');
    return;
  }

  handOver('a reply that is none of the four cases this workflow acts on by itself',
    numbers.length ? `Invoice(s) mentioned: ${numbers.join(', ')}` : '');
});

return out;

parameters.message:
={{ $('Read What the Reply Says').item.json.from }} disputes invoice {{ $('Read What the Reply Says').item.json.invoice_number }}.

Their reason: {{ $('Read What the Reply Says').item.json.dispute_reason }}

Subject: {{ $('Read What the Reply Says').item.json.subject }}

The invoice is marked disputed in the sheet and no further chaser will go out on it. Clearing the status is what starts the clock again.

=A customer replied and the workflow did not act on it alone.

From:    {{ $json.from }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject }}
Reading: {{ $json.intent }}

Why you have it: {{ $json.why }}

{{ $json.detail }}

Nothing has been written to the sheet, so whatever you do next is the first thing that happens to this invoice.

=A run of the collections workflow stopped with an error.

Error:     {{ $json.execution.error.message }}
At node:   {{ $json.execution.lastNodeExecuted }}
Execution: {{ $json.execution.url }}

Nothing partial is left behind: the chase log is written per customer, so whoever was already emailed has a row, and the next run reads those rows and leaves them alone.
